    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d369">

                <pb facs="0628" n="608" sameAs="frus:frus1864p2/pg608"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Lord Lyons.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>,<hi
                                rendition="#italic"> Washington</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-05-14"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >May</hi> 14, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Lord</hi>: Recurring to your note of the 30th
                    ultimo, respecting the detention of Percival A. Bedwell and four others, taken
                    on the steamer Don, and to your note of the 29th ultimo, relative to persons
                    similarly situated at Fortress Monroe, I have the honor to enclose, for your
                    lordship’s information, a copy of a letter of the 7th instant on the subject
                    from the Navy Department, and to be, with high consideration, my lord, your
                    obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Right Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lord Lyons.</hi></p>
                </postscript>


                <xi:include href="d369-a1.xml" xpointer="d369-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
